    "https://tru.hua.hrsmart.com/hr/ats/Posting/view/35276": {
      "title": "CRM Analyst - (00543.2)",
      "description": "Jump to main content Attention Safari users: This site requires cookies to function. Please click here to accept the cookie. Cookies will be used strictly for the functioning of the site. Toggle navigation Job Search View All Jobs Create Account Log in Help Help on this Page Job Details CRM Analyst - (00543.2) Share this job as a link in your status update to LinkedIn. Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Support Staff (CUPE) Posting In effect from 24/8/2026 Closing Application Date 4/9/2026 Closing date for internal CUPE applicants 4/9/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” and may continue until the position is filled. Internal CUPE applicants must submit their application by 4pm on the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” for their Seniority to be recognized. Applications received after the \"closing date for internal CUPE applicants\" will be considered alongside external applicants. Full/Part Time Full Time Support Type Anticipated Start Date 1/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 28/2/2027 The Hours of work are subject to change depending upon departmental requirements Schedule The hours of work will be Monday to Friday, 7 hours a day, 8:00 am to 4:00 pm (subject to change depending upon departmental requirements) Schedule Description The hours of work will be Monday to Friday, 7 hours a day DUTIES The CRM Analyst plays a crucial role in ensuring the smooth operation and support of TRU’s information technology infrastructure. Reporting to the Associate Director, Enterprise Systems, this position focuses on delivering exceptional service and support for TRU’s Customer Relationships Management (CRM) systems and various aspects of other Enterprise systems. MAJOR DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Provides system administration support to CRM and other core enterprise systems. Regularly engages in problem solving in both a technical and non-technical sense at various levels of the university such as with technical staff, managers, clients, and external partner organizations. Builds, installs, and customizes new CRM applications and systems, maintaining and enhancing existing applications and systems. Develops packages, programs, and scripts supporting CRM and other Enterprise systems. Supports standard reporting tools and creates various reports to meet end-user requirements. Designs and implements integrations between CRM, ERP, and other enterprise systems. Conducts research, evaluation and prototyping of new and innovative technologies. Recommends CRM and related systems strategies, methodology, programming directions and architecture, and implementation paths for risk mitigation strategies. Contributes development projects for CRM and other enterprise systems. Works closely with cross-functional teams and business units to align CRM strategies with business objectives. Conducts reviews of systems, application designs, implementation plans and interfacing structures to ensure overall quality and conformance of information technology to industry and TRU standards as well as applicable legislations. Develops operating standards, policies and procedures for staff, contractor(s) and consultant(s) working in our technology environments or within institution-guided technology-orientated projects. Monitoring and establishing quality control guidelines, ensuring standards compliance, and monitoring resource usage. Provides consultation, advice, and training to users of the institution’s critical CRM systems and other Enterprise systems. Develops and delivers training materials, system documentation and technical presentations for the purpose of demonstrating systems and training. Produces programming and systems documentation for existing systems and new implementations. Maintains currency of technical knowledge by training, cross-training and researching. REPORTS TO Associate Director, Enterprise Systems QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: A Bachelor’s degree in an Information Technology discipline such as Computer Science, Business Administration, or equivalent EXPERIENCE: Four years recent and related experience SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE OR ABILITIES RELATED TO THE JOB Demonstrated knowledge of the Systems Development Life Cycle and respective methodologies Demonstrated knowledge and skill of reporting and business intelligence tools Demonstrated knowledge and skill of data analysis Demonstrated knowledge of RDBMS such as Oracle and Microsoft database solutions Knowledge and skill in software development Knowledge of ERP and complex information systems Demonstrated proficiency in CRM software Ability to deal with users, coworkers and external vendors with courtesy, discretion and tact; dealing with difficult situations appropriately Ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing Ability to plan and organize work Ability to exercise considerable independent action Ability to apply continuous mental effort for long periods of time Demonstrated ability to develop systems specifications Adaptability and willingness to learn new technologies and methodologies WORKING CONDITIONS Sitting at a desk and computer for long periods of time Visiting client locations General office condition The salary for the above position is determined by the Collective Agreement with the Canadian Union of Public Employees, Local 4879, as it presently exists. Pay Band $34.07 - $37.86 ( CUPE Grade 09 (90% - 100%) ) Salary rate This Position is not subject to a 90% start rate for new Employees. Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Information Technology Services -> Enterprise Systems Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job v18.5.3 Last sync: 2026-09-03 22:50:04 Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Support Staff (CUPE) Posting In effect from 24/8/2026 Closing Application Date 4/9/2026 Closing date for internal CUPE applicants 4/9/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” and may continue until the position is filled. Internal CUPE applicants must submit their application by 4pm on the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” for their Seniority to be recognized. Applications received after the \"closing date for internal CUPE applicants\" will be considered alongside external applicants. Full/Part Time Full Time Support Type Anticipated Start Date 1/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 28/2/2027 The Hours of work are subject to change depending upon departmental requirements Schedule The hours of work will be Monday to Friday, 7 hours a day, 8:00 am to 4:00 pm (subject to change depending upon departmental requirements) Schedule Description The hours of work will be Monday to Friday, 7 hours a day DUTIES The CRM Analyst plays a crucial role in ensuring the smooth operation and support of TRU’s information technology infrastructure. Reporting to the Associate Director, Enterprise Systems, this position focuses on delivering exceptional service and support for TRU’s Customer Relationships Management (CRM) systems and various aspects of other Enterprise systems. MAJOR DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Provides system administration support to CRM and other core enterprise systems. Regularly engages in problem solving in both a technical and non-technical sense at various levels of the university such as with technical staff, managers, clients, and external partner organizations. Builds, installs, and customizes new CRM applications and systems, maintaining and enhancing existing applications and systems. Develops packages, programs, and scripts supporting CRM and other Enterprise systems. Supports standard reporting tools and creates various reports to meet end-user requirements. Designs and implements integrations between CRM, ERP, and other enterprise systems. Conducts research, evaluation and prototyping of new and innovative technologies. Recommends CRM and related systems strategies, methodology, programming directions and architecture, and implementation paths for risk mitigation strategies. Contributes development projects for CRM and other enterprise systems. Works closely with cross-functional teams and business units to align CRM strategies with business objectives. Conducts reviews of systems, application designs, implementation plans and interfacing structures to ensure overall quality and conformance of information technology to industry and TRU standards as well as applicable legislations. Develops operating standards, policies and procedures for staff, contractor(s) and consultant(s) working in our technology environments or within institution-guided technology-orientated projects. Monitoring and establishing quality control guidelines, ensuring standards compliance, and monitoring resource usage. Provides consultation, advice, and training to users of the institution’s critical CRM systems and other Enterprise systems. Develops and delivers training materials, system documentation and technical presentations for the purpose of demonstrating systems and training. Produces programming and systems documentation for existing systems and new implementations. Maintains currency of technical knowledge by training, cross-training and researching. REPORTS TO Associate Director, Enterprise Systems QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: A Bachelor’s degree in an Information Technology discipline such as Computer Science, Business Administration, or equivalent EXPERIENCE: Four years recent and related experience SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE OR ABILITIES RELATED TO THE JOB Demonstrated knowledge of the Systems Development Life Cycle and respective methodologies Demonstrated knowledge and skill of reporting and business intelligence tools Demonstrated knowledge and skill of data analysis Demonstrated knowledge of RDBMS such as Oracle and Microsoft database solutions Knowledge and skill in software development Knowledge of ERP and complex information systems Demonstrated proficiency in CRM software Ability to deal with users, coworkers and external vendors with courtesy, discretion and tact; dealing with difficult situations appropriately Ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing Ability to plan and organize work Ability to exercise considerable independent action Ability to apply continuous mental effort for long periods of time Demonstrated ability to develop systems specifications Adaptability and willingness to learn new technologies and methodologies WORKING CONDITIONS Sitting at a desk and computer for long periods of time Visiting client locations General office condition The salary for the above position is determined by the Collective Agreement with the Canadian Union of Public Employees, Local 4879, as it presently exists. Pay Band $34.07 - $37.86 ( CUPE Grade 09 (90% - 100%) ) Salary rate This Position is not subject to a 90% start rate for new Employees. Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Information Technology Services -> Enterprise Systems Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job"
