    "https://tru.hua.hrsmart.com/hr/ats/Posting/view/35130": {
      "title": "Clerk/Receptionist - (Facilities) - (00197.23)",
      "description": "Jump to main content Attention Safari users: This site requires cookies to function. Please click here to accept the cookie. Cookies will be used strictly for the functioning of the site. Toggle navigation Job Search View All Jobs Create Account Log in Help Help on this Page Job Details Clerk/Receptionist - (Facilities) - (00197.23) Share this job as a link in your status update to LinkedIn. Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Support Staff (CUPE) Posting In effect from 6/8/2026 Closing Application Date 19/8/2026 Closing date for internal CUPE applicants 19/8/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” and may continue until the position is filled. Internal CUPE applicants must submit their application by 4pm on the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” for their Seniority to be recognized. Applications received after the \"closing date for internal CUPE applicants\" will be considered alongside external applicants. Full/Part Time Full Time Support Type Anticipated Start Date 1/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 28/9/2027 The Hours of work are subject to change depending upon departmental requirements Schedule The hours of work will be Monday to Friday, 7 hours a day, 8:30 am to 4:30 pm (subject to change depending upon departmental requirements) Schedule Description DUTIES Performs a variety of clerical and receptionist functions such as performing electronic data entry, maintaining parking control, maintaining vehicle database and key distribution systems, receiving and distributing mail, answering the telephone and responding to counter inquiries and providing secretarial support for the department. MAJOR DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Provides receptionist duties by receiving visitors, providing information and directing to appropriate area; answers the telephone, directs calls and takes messages. Compiles parking permits inventory on spreadsheets; issues parking permits and e-permits as required for staff and students; maintains records of parking violations; collects fines, maintains cash float and issues receipts. Maintains a vehicle fleet database by handling requests, booking vehicles, preparing schedules and completing the necessary documentation; keys related information and prepare spreadsheets. Maintains a key inventory and control system by handling requests, ordering, receiving and issuing keys, and updating electronic and manual records. Liaises with external parking contractors to maintain and monitor systems such as multi-space machines, and parking control gates. Works with the insurance broker to arrange and maintain TRU fleet vehicle insurance. Works with IT Services to develop parking application system and handle associated difficulties. Processes application forms for bike compound keys and distribute keys to students and staff. Types routine correspondence; sets up and maintains files; receives, sorts and distributes internal mail; compiles data and prepares reports. Take minutes or notes and provides information on parking violations at Parking Appeal Committee meetings. Maintains departmental office supplies and equipment. Trains general office overload and relief personnel. Perform duties of Facilities Services Clerk such as receiving and handling problem maintenance calls and responding to emergencies, generating work control documents and time sheets. REPORTS TO Director, Facilities QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: Grade 12 plus two years’ post-secondary education or equivalent EXPERIENCE: Three years’ related experience, including one year of experience with electronic word processing and data entry SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE OR ABILITIES RELATED TO THE JOB Ability to perform electronic word processing at 60 wpm and data entry The proven ability to take and transcribe minutes and correspondence at 70 verbal wpm Ability to deal courteously and tactfully with others including students, staff and members of the general public Ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing Ability to organize work Ability to operate related equipment such as photocopier, 2-way radio and pager system WORKING CONDITIONS Working at computer and desk, front counter work; general office conditions Sitting/standing for long periods of time The salary for the above position is determined by the Collective Agreement with the Canadian Union of Public Employees, Local 4879, as it presently exists. Pay Band $30.98 - $34.42 ( CUPE Grade 07 (90% - 100%) ) Salary rate This Position is not subject to a 90% start rate for new Employees. Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Campus Infrastructure and Sustainability -> Parking Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job v18.5.3 Last sync: 2026-09-03 22:50:04 Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Support Staff (CUPE) Posting In effect from 6/8/2026 Closing Application Date 19/8/2026 Closing date for internal CUPE applicants 19/8/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” and may continue until the position is filled. Internal CUPE applicants must submit their application by 4pm on the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” for their Seniority to be recognized. Applications received after the \"closing date for internal CUPE applicants\" will be considered alongside external applicants. Full/Part Time Full Time Support Type Anticipated Start Date 1/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 28/9/2027 The Hours of work are subject to change depending upon departmental requirements Schedule The hours of work will be Monday to Friday, 7 hours a day, 8:30 am to 4:30 pm (subject to change depending upon departmental requirements) Schedule Description DUTIES Performs a variety of clerical and receptionist functions such as performing electronic data entry, maintaining parking control, maintaining vehicle database and key distribution systems, receiving and distributing mail, answering the telephone and responding to counter inquiries and providing secretarial support for the department. MAJOR DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Provides receptionist duties by receiving visitors, providing information and directing to appropriate area; answers the telephone, directs calls and takes messages. Compiles parking permits inventory on spreadsheets; issues parking permits and e-permits as required for staff and students; maintains records of parking violations; collects fines, maintains cash float and issues receipts. Maintains a vehicle fleet database by handling requests, booking vehicles, preparing schedules and completing the necessary documentation; keys related information and prepare spreadsheets. Maintains a key inventory and control system by handling requests, ordering, receiving and issuing keys, and updating electronic and manual records. Liaises with external parking contractors to maintain and monitor systems such as multi-space machines, and parking control gates. Works with the insurance broker to arrange and maintain TRU fleet vehicle insurance. Works with IT Services to develop parking application system and handle associated difficulties. Processes application forms for bike compound keys and distribute keys to students and staff. Types routine correspondence; sets up and maintains files; receives, sorts and distributes internal mail; compiles data and prepares reports. Take minutes or notes and provides information on parking violations at Parking Appeal Committee meetings. Maintains departmental office supplies and equipment. Trains general office overload and relief personnel. Perform duties of Facilities Services Clerk such as receiving and handling problem maintenance calls and responding to emergencies, generating work control documents and time sheets. REPORTS TO Director, Facilities QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: Grade 12 plus two years’ post-secondary education or equivalent EXPERIENCE: Three years’ related experience, including one year of experience with electronic word processing and data entry SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE OR ABILITIES RELATED TO THE JOB Ability to perform electronic word processing at 60 wpm and data entry The proven ability to take and transcribe minutes and correspondence at 70 verbal wpm Ability to deal courteously and tactfully with others including students, staff and members of the general public Ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing Ability to organize work Ability to operate related equipment such as photocopier, 2-way radio and pager system WORKING CONDITIONS Working at computer and desk, front counter work; general office conditions Sitting/standing for long periods of time The salary for the above position is determined by the Collective Agreement with the Canadian Union of Public Employees, Local 4879, as it presently exists. Pay Band $30.98 - $34.42 ( CUPE Grade 07 (90% - 100%) ) Salary rate This Position is not subject to a 90% start rate for new Employees. Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Campus Infrastructure and Sustainability -> Parking Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job"
    },
    "https://tru.hua.hrsmart.com/hr/ats/Posting/view/35058": {
      "title": "Senior Communications Consultant, Marketing and Communications - (01264.13)",
      "description": "Jump to main content Attention Safari users: This site requires cookies to function. Please click here to accept the cookie. Cookies will be used strictly for the functioning of the site. Toggle navigation Job Search View All Jobs Create Account Log in Help Help on this Page Job Details Senior Communications Consultant, Marketing and Communications - (01264.13) Share this job as a link in your status update to LinkedIn. Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Administrative/Management Posting In effect from 5/8/2026 Closing Application Date 19/8/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the closing application date and may continue until the position is filled. Full/Part Time Full Time Admin Type Ongoing Anticipated Start Date 14/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) DUTIES The Senior Communications Consultant is an experienced professional who will provide communications support for the university's senior leadership team under the direction of the Associate Director, Strategic Communications. The Senior Communications Officer will function as a generalist, having the ability to provide a range of communication services that support communications to both internal and external audiences. Such services may include communication planning, media relations, event coordination, and writing for internal and external channels, including social media. Work priorities will be determined in consultation with the Associate Director, Strategic Communications. MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES Provide strategic advice and tactical communications support for various initiatives stemming from the university's senior leadership team or their direct reports. Regularly liaise with various units that report up to the senior leadership team to keep abreast of initiatives, issues, and seek opportunities for proactive communications. Build and maintain a positive image for the university through the proactive communication of initiatives to a variety of stakeholders through strategic communication plan development, and at times, through issues management under the direction of the Associate Director, Strategic Communications. Manage and update the internal and external website presence of members of the senior leadership team, and specific projects pages under the direction of the Associate Director. Provide communications-related workshops, including media training, in collaboration with the Associate Director, Strategic Communications. Support response to media queries during the day, and after-hours when needed. Assist the Associate Director, Strategic Communications on major institutional announcements and events, including support with communications material development, gathering information and fact checking. Support the Associate Director with crisis communications as required. Provide communications support to the senior leadership team, under the guidance of the Associate Vice-President Marketing & Communications, in the Associate Director's absence. REPORTS TO Associate Director, Strategic Communications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE/SKILLS EDUCATION: A Bachelor's degree in journalism, communications, or a related discipline EXPERIENCE: Seven (7) years working in a communications-related field Experience working with middle and senior management level leaders preferred Proven ability to produce and implement communications plans A proven track record in a complex, multi-stakeholder, fast-paced environment Strong writing skills, with attention to accuracy, and detail Ability to write in varied tones and formats, to reach diverse stakeholder audiences Experience in internal and external communications, media relations and issues management. Demonstrated skills in social media channels Strong organizational skills and ability to handle multiple projects simultaneously Ability to work independently, and within a team Proven track record in handling sensitive and confidential issues with tact and diplomacy Experience with Microsoft Office Pay Band $87,001.00 - $99,151.00 ( Admin Pay Band BH ) Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Marketing and Communications Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job v18.5.3 Last sync: 2026-09-03 22:50:04 Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Administrative/Management Posting In effect from 5/8/2026 Closing Application Date 19/8/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the closing application date and may continue until the position is filled. Full/Part Time Full Time Admin Type Ongoing Anticipated Start Date 14/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) DUTIES The Senior Communications Consultant is an experienced professional who will provide communications support for the university's senior leadership team under the direction of the Associate Director, Strategic Communications. The Senior Communications Officer will function as a generalist, having the ability to provide a range of communication services that support communications to both internal and external audiences. Such services may include communication planning, media relations, event coordination, and writing for internal and external channels, including social media. Work priorities will be determined in consultation with the Associate Director, Strategic Communications. MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES Provide strategic advice and tactical communications support for various initiatives stemming from the university's senior leadership team or their direct reports. Regularly liaise with various units that report up to the senior leadership team to keep abreast of initiatives, issues, and seek opportunities for proactive communications. Build and maintain a positive image for the university through the proactive communication of initiatives to a variety of stakeholders through strategic communication plan development, and at times, through issues management under the direction of the Associate Director, Strategic Communications. Manage and update the internal and external website presence of members of the senior leadership team, and specific projects pages under the direction of the Associate Director. Provide communications-related workshops, including media training, in collaboration with the Associate Director, Strategic Communications. Support response to media queries during the day, and after-hours when needed. Assist the Associate Director, Strategic Communications on major institutional announcements and events, including support with communications material development, gathering information and fact checking. Support the Associate Director with crisis communications as required. Provide communications support to the senior leadership team, under the guidance of the Associate Vice-President Marketing & Communications, in the Associate Director's absence. REPORTS TO Associate Director, Strategic Communications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE/SKILLS EDUCATION: A Bachelor's degree in journalism, communications, or a related discipline EXPERIENCE: Seven (7) years working in a communications-related field Experience working with middle and senior management level leaders preferred Proven ability to produce and implement communications plans A proven track record in a complex, multi-stakeholder, fast-paced environment Strong writing skills, with attention to accuracy, and detail Ability to write in varied tones and formats, to reach diverse stakeholder audiences Experience in internal and external communications, media relations and issues management. Demonstrated skills in social media channels Strong organizational skills and ability to handle multiple projects simultaneously Ability to work independently, and within a team Proven track record in handling sensitive and confidential issues with tact and diplomacy Experience with Microsoft Office Pay Band $87,001.00 - $99,151.00 ( Admin Pay Band BH ) Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Marketing and Communications Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job"
