    "https://tru.hua.hrsmart.com/hr/ats/Posting/view/35030": {
      "title": "Clinical Resource Coordinator - Respiratory Therapy - (02056.286)",
      "description": "Jump to main content Attention Safari users: This site requires cookies to function. Please click here to accept the cookie. Cookies will be used strictly for the functioning of the site. Toggle navigation Job Search View All Jobs Create Account Log in Help Help on this Page Job Details Clinical Resource Coordinator - Respiratory Therapy - (02056.286) Share this job as a link in your status update to LinkedIn. Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Faculty (Sessional) Posting In effect from 24/7/2026 Closing Application Date 10/8/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the closing application date and may continue until the position is filled. Instructional Type Instructional Support Anticipated Start Date 8/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 31/8/2027 DUTIES Thompson Rivers University invites applications for an on-going part-time clinical resource coordinator role in the Respiratory Therapy Program, Allied Health Department, Faculty of Science. The successful candidate will be expected to provide both instruction (teaching) and instructional support to TRU RT program students and Clinical Site Coordinators (CSC) during the clinical practicum year. Most of this support will be provided via distance, as the candidate will need to support clinical sites throughout all the BC health authorities. Some in-person requirements may be required, such as participating in program operational meetings. These in-person meetings would most likely occur in both Kamloops and the Lower Mainland. The candidate will be expected to provide multiple forms of support, with the overall goal of enhancing the consistency and quality of learning and operational resources for students and clinical faculty. Some examples include maintaining and updating online competency tracking tools, online exam banks, Moodle courses, student and CSC handbooks, orientation resources, standardized exams, and other forms of support as they relate to ongoing program quality assurance and quality improvement. The department is seeking a faculty member with educator experience who can demonstrate effective teamwork, communication, and organizational skills. Evidence of how the candidate has lead projects will be required, with emphasis placed on self-direction, consensus building, and ability to meet deadlines. Preferences will be given to those who can demonstrate online educator experience and project management involving multiple health authorities or diverse groups. QUALIFICATIONS Baccalaureate degree in relevant discipline RRT credential from an accredited Canadian program Minimum 3 years of recent clinical experience (time as a clinical student will NOT count towards the years) Minimum of one year teaching/educator experience. Experience can occur in a variety of formats but must be more than preceptoring students at a bedside. Examples may include staff educator, clinical site coordinator, simulation educator, or regional or professional practice educator. Proficient at using and managing online learning management tools, Moodle preferred Evidence of effective teamwork and constructive communication skills Evidence of effectively leading projects Additional considerations will be given to candidates with one or more of the following: Clinical site coordinator experience Respiratory therapy staff educator experience Evidence of teaching students via online learning platforms (e.g. Moodle) Evidence of project management involving multiple health authorities or diverse groups Pay Band $78,152.00 - $198,763.00 ( According to TRUFA Salary Schedule (Range TS01 - TS35) ) Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Faculty of Science -> Respiratory Therapy Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job v18.5.3 Last sync: 2026-09-03 22:55:04 Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Faculty (Sessional) Posting In effect from 24/7/2026 Closing Application Date 10/8/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the closing application date and may continue until the position is filled. Instructional Type Instructional Support Anticipated Start Date 8/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 31/8/2027 DUTIES Thompson Rivers University invites applications for an on-going part-time clinical resource coordinator role in the Respiratory Therapy Program, Allied Health Department, Faculty of Science. The successful candidate will be expected to provide both instruction (teaching) and instructional support to TRU RT program students and Clinical Site Coordinators (CSC) during the clinical practicum year. Most of this support will be provided via distance, as the candidate will need to support clinical sites throughout all the BC health authorities. Some in-person requirements may be required, such as participating in program operational meetings. These in-person meetings would most likely occur in both Kamloops and the Lower Mainland. The candidate will be expected to provide multiple forms of support, with the overall goal of enhancing the consistency and quality of learning and operational resources for students and clinical faculty. Some examples include maintaining and updating online competency tracking tools, online exam banks, Moodle courses, student and CSC handbooks, orientation resources, standardized exams, and other forms of support as they relate to ongoing program quality assurance and quality improvement. The department is seeking a faculty member with educator experience who can demonstrate effective teamwork, communication, and organizational skills. Evidence of how the candidate has lead projects will be required, with emphasis placed on self-direction, consensus building, and ability to meet deadlines. Preferences will be given to those who can demonstrate online educator experience and project management involving multiple health authorities or diverse groups. QUALIFICATIONS Baccalaureate degree in relevant discipline RRT credential from an accredited Canadian program Minimum 3 years of recent clinical experience (time as a clinical student will NOT count towards the years) Minimum of one year teaching/educator experience. Experience can occur in a variety of formats but must be more than preceptoring students at a bedside. Examples may include staff educator, clinical site coordinator, simulation educator, or regional or professional practice educator. Proficient at using and managing online learning management tools, Moodle preferred Evidence of effective teamwork and constructive communication skills Evidence of effectively leading projects Additional considerations will be given to candidates with one or more of the following: Clinical site coordinator experience Respiratory therapy staff educator experience Evidence of teaching students via online learning platforms (e.g. Moodle) Evidence of project management involving multiple health authorities or diverse groups Pay Band $78,152.00 - $198,763.00 ( According to TRUFA Salary Schedule (Range TS01 - TS35) ) Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Faculty of Science -> Respiratory Therapy Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job"
