    "https://tru.hua.hrsmart.com/hr/ats/Posting/view/34966": {
      "title": "Sessional - Faculty (CNCS 1110, 1150, 1160, 2170, 1210, 1220, 1230, 1240, 1250, 1260, 1270) - (02050.11835)",
      "description": "Jump to main content Attention Safari users: This site requires cookies to function. Please click here to accept the cookie. Cookies will be used strictly for the functioning of the site. Toggle navigation Job Search View All Jobs Create Account Log in Help Help on this Page Job Details Sessional - Faculty (CNCS 1110, 1150, 1160, 2170, 1210, 1220, 1230, 1240, 1250, 1260, 1270) - (02050.11835) Share this job as a link in your status update to LinkedIn. Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Faculty (Sessional) Posting In effect from 21/7/2026 Closing Application Date 4/8/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the closing application date and may continue until the position is filled. Instructional Type Academic/Career(max 24 credits) Anticipated Start Date 7/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 7/5/2027 DUTIES The Department of Data Science requires a sessional instructor to teach a variety of courses in the Cybersecurity program. These courses may include areas such as foundational computing studies, Python programming, cybersecurity fundamentals, ethical hacking, database basics, operating systems security, Linux and Windows basics, networking, virtualization, infrastructure design, and integrated security practices. Duties include delivering lectures, labs, and seminars, as well as marking assignments, quizzes, tests, and examinations. The course is already developed and has been offered on a regular basis. The successful candidate will be responsible for facilitating student learning through classroom instruction, laboratory activities, and practical exercises focused on Python programming and cybersecurity applications. The ability to teach in this area and contribute to student success in an applied learning environment will be considered an asset. Other courses may be assigned depending on departmental needs and the qualifications and expertise of the candidate. Thompson Rivers University (TRU), www.tru.ca, is a uniquely comprehensive and student-focused institution built on over 50 years of excellence in post-secondary education and training. Located in Kamloops, British Columbia, TRU offers a dynamic learning and research environment that combines academic excellence, innovation, and strong community connections. Kamloops provides outstanding recreational, cultural, social, and economic opportunities and enjoys more than 2,000 hours of sunshine annually. QUALIFICATIONS Master's degree in Cybersecurity, Computer Science, Data Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated knowledge of key areas in cybersecurity, including fundamentals, ethical hacking, operating systems security, Linux and Windows security basics, networking, virtualization, infrastructure design, integrated security practices, and Python programming as applied to cybersecurity. University-level teaching experience in programming, cybersecurity, network security, or related computing courses. Evidence of teaching effectiveness through teaching evaluations, curriculum development, instructional innovation, or a teaching dossier. Experience with applied cybersecurity tools, secure coding practices, and hands-on laboratory instruction. Strong communication skills and fluency in spoken and written English. Pay Band $2,732.34 - $2,732.34 ( Sessional Faculty - Academic (per credit) ) Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Faculty of Science -> Computing Science Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job v18.5.3 Last sync: 2026-09-03 22:55:04 Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Faculty (Sessional) Posting In effect from 21/7/2026 Closing Application Date 4/8/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the closing application date and may continue until the position is filled. Instructional Type Academic/Career(max 24 credits) Anticipated Start Date 7/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 7/5/2027 DUTIES The Department of Data Science requires a sessional instructor to teach a variety of courses in the Cybersecurity program. These courses may include areas such as foundational computing studies, Python programming, cybersecurity fundamentals, ethical hacking, database basics, operating systems security, Linux and Windows basics, networking, virtualization, infrastructure design, and integrated security practices. Duties include delivering lectures, labs, and seminars, as well as marking assignments, quizzes, tests, and examinations. The course is already developed and has been offered on a regular basis. The successful candidate will be responsible for facilitating student learning through classroom instruction, laboratory activities, and practical exercises focused on Python programming and cybersecurity applications. The ability to teach in this area and contribute to student success in an applied learning environment will be considered an asset. Other courses may be assigned depending on departmental needs and the qualifications and expertise of the candidate. Thompson Rivers University (TRU), ww