    "https://tru.hua.hrsmart.com/hr/ats/Posting/view/34891": {
      "title": "Sessional - Faculty RESP 2590; RESP 2680; RESP 2570 - (02050.11814)",
      "description": "Jump to main content Attention Safari users: This site requires cookies to function. Please click here to accept the cookie. Cookies will be used strictly for the functioning of the site. Toggle navigation Job Search View All Jobs Create Account Log in Help Help on this Page Job Details Sessional - Faculty RESP 2590; RESP 2680; RESP 2570 - (02050.11814) Share this job as a link in your status update to LinkedIn. Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Faculty (Sessional) Posting In effect from 2/7/2026 Closing Application Date 15/7/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the closing application date and may continue until the position is filled. Instructional Type Academic/Career(max 24 credits) Anticipated Start Date 8/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 8/12/2026 DUTIES The successful candidates will prepare and teach one or more of the following: RESP 2570 – Blood Gas Analysis Lab (3 credits total) LO7- Every Tuesday 1730- 1920 (1 credit) LO1 – Every Thursday1330-1520 (1 credit) LO2 – Every Thursday 1530-1720 (1 credit) RESP 2590 – Patient Assessment Lab (1 credit total) LO2 – Every Monday 1530-1720 (1 credit) RESP 2680 – Pulmonary Function Lab (1 credit total) LO3 - Every Thursday starting Oct 22 1330-1520 (0.5 credits) LO4 - Every Thursday starting Oct 22 1530-1720 (0.5 credits) Additionally, each candidate: Must be able to reliably communicate with the primary course instructor to ensure they are aware of each labs expectations and learning outcomes. This will require review of lab content prior to each lab. Will be expected be available to assist with lab exams based on the lab. While the exact dates and times for each lab exam are not yet finalized, please assume the following: For Patient Assessment (RESP 2590) & Blood Gas Analysis (RESP 2570), the final days of class/labs are Dec 7 & 8 (Mon & Tues). There is a high chance that lab exams will occur on these days. It is expected each candidate can be available on Dec 7 & 8. If that is not possible it must be indicated during the application. Not being available does not prevent taking a section but may factor into selection. For Pulmonary Function (RESP 2680), the lab exams are expected to take place during regularly schedule lab times near the end of the semester. Additionally, there is a high likelihood lab exams will take place outside of regularly scheduled lab hours, but any participation in these additional times will be discussed with candidates to see if they are available to assist with. QUALIFICATIONS • RRT credential • Evidence of effective teaching/preceptoring experience • Evidence of effective teamwork and constructive communication skills Pay Band $2,732.34 - $2,732.34 ( Sessional Faculty - Academic (per credit) ) Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Faculty of Science -> Respiratory Therapy Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job v18.5.3 Last sync: 2026-09-03 22:55:04 Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Faculty (Sessional) Posting In effect from 2/7/2026 Closing Application Date 15/7/