    "https://tru.hua.hrsmart.com/hr/ats/Posting/view/34779": {
      "title": "Curriculum Multimedia Developer - (00230.16)",
      "description": "Jump to main content Attention Safari users: This site requires cookies to function. Please click here to accept the cookie. Cookies will be used strictly for the functioning of the site. Toggle navigation Job Search View All Jobs Create Account Log in Help Help on this Page Job Details Curriculum Multimedia Developer - (00230.16) Application Restrictions For Internal Candidates Only Job Type Support Staff (CUPE) Posting In effect from 17/6/2026 Closing Application Date 2/7/2026 Closing date for internal CUPE applicants 2/7/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” and may continue until the position is filled. Internal CUPE applicants must submit their application by 4pm on the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” for their Seniority to be recognized. Applications received after the \"closing date for internal CUPE applicants\" will be considered alongside external applicants. Full/Part Time Full Time Support Type Anticipated Start Date 1/8/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 31/7/2028 The Hours of work are subject to change depending upon departmental requirements Schedule The hours of work will be Monday to Friday, 7 hours a day, 8:00 am to 4:00 pm (subject to change depending upon departmental requirements) Schedule Description DUTIES **NOTE:  This position is subject to review by the Joint Job Evaluation Committee** The Curriculum Multimedia Developer develops and deploys online interactive instructional multimedia for Open Learning courses and other on-campus groups.  This position supports and collaborates with other media and production specialists. The position manages the development and implementation of interactive multimedia in a variety of online formats. The Curriculum Multimedia Developer supports Instructional Designers, subject matter experts, and other faculty and staff with learning technologies and educational media. MAJOR DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Designs, develops, produces and coordinates implementation of responsive cross-platform interactive instructional multimedia and learning environments for Open Learning and campus, ensuring that they are fully adaptable to a wide variety of devices. Finds, repurposes and/or develops open educational multimedia resources under Creative Commons and related regimes; makes recommendations and participates in the development of storage and content sharing tools with the use of metadata systems and repositories. Oversees final implementation and quality control of multimedia, including testing and adjustments as necessary to ensure proper functioning of interactive multimedia including in live server environments. Supports and collaborates with graphics designer and video producer to achieve coordinated approaches to media development and implementation including providing assistance with basic video and graphic tasks when required. Based on a broad and in-depth knowledge of instructional media and technology, analyzes needs and makes recommendations to Instructional Designers, subject matter experts, faculty and staff on pedagogically sound interactive multimedia for online courses, programs and other educational offerings. Participates in course and program planning teams related to new development and maintenance of existing curriculum or other education focused projects, including handling of issues related to coordinating, scheduling and managing implementation of multiple projects under time-sensitive conditions. Utilizes project-tracking software and participates in constant quality improvement of  media team workflows related to the work with Instructional Design, Editing, Copyright and Production teams as well as campus clients . Operates in server environments for testing, production, and hosting of interactive educational multimedia, and communicates with technical server specialists concerning needs related to the smooth functioning and updating of host environments. Builds capacity in interactive multimedia by developing and delivering workshops and other hands-on training for campus and online faculty. Supports the Learning Technology and Innovation Team by identifying, analyzing, testing, evaluating, and reporting on existing and emerging learning media technologies and their appropriateness for use in online courses and programs, and in training others in the use of these technologies. Participates in relevant conferences by attending and presenting on practices and emerging developments in Open Learning and educational media. REPORTS TO Manager, Learning Technology and Innovation QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: Bachelor's degree in related field such as Digital Media/Arts; Learning Technologies; Instructional Development; Information Technology EXPERIENCE: Five years' related experience in an interactive multimedia role, including: Three years' experience in educational multi-media Two years working in a complex development and production setting requiring strong project management and coordination skills SKILLS KNOWLEDGE OR ABILITIES RELATED TO THE JOB Demonstrated proficiency in the following programing environments HTML5, CSS, JavaScript, PHP Demonstrated proficiency in user interface design and ability to create in multiple media formats (audio, video, and graphics) Demonstrated skills in e-learning, collaboration, and communication software such as WordPress, H5P, Articulate Storyline and Adobe Captivate Ability to create and edit sound, video and graphics media Ability to perform effectively as part of a project development team Ability to interpret curriculum requirements into appropriate educational interactive applications for LMS/external environments Communication and conflict management skills that are effective, courteous and tactful Ability to manage timelines using project management software for multiple concurrent and complex projects Ability to exercise considerable independent action and make sound decisions Advanced understanding of user interface design, media formats (audio, video, and graphics), and appropriate computer applications (e.g. current and emerging technologies) Understanding of how audio is recorded properly. Advanced knowledge of Adobe Creative Cloud suite Familiary with Camtasia video software Ability to operate in Windows server environment, web servers, , remote desk protocols and maintain best practices in workflow and file management Ability to work in Learning Management Systems (LMSs) e.g. Moodle Ability to use MS Office Suite WORKING CONDITIONS Sitting at a computer and desk for long periods of time General office conditions The salary for the above position is determined by the Collective Agreement with the Canadian Union of Public Employees, Local 4879, as it presently exists. Pay Band $34.07 - $37.86 ( CUPE Grade 09 (90% - 100%) ) Salary rate Please Note: This position may be subject to a 90% salary for the first 560 hours of employment. Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Open, Learning, Teaching and Innovation -> Innovations – OL Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job v18.5.3 Last sync: 2026-09-03 22:55:04 Application Restrictions For Internal Candidates Only Job Type Support Staff (CUPE) Posting In effect from 17/6/2026 Closing Application Date 2/7/2026 Closing date for internal CUPE applicants 2/7/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” and may continue until the position is filled. Internal CUPE applicants must submit their application by 4pm on the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” for their Seniority to be recognized. Applications received after the \"closing date for internal CUPE applicants\" will be considered alongside external applicants. Full/Part Time Full Time Support Type Anticipated Start Date 1/8/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 31/7/2028 The Hours of work are subject to change depending upon departmental requirements Schedule The hours of work will be Monday to Friday, 7 hours a day, 8:00 am to 4:00 pm (subject to change depending upon departmental requirements) Schedule Description DUTIES **NOTE:  This position is subject to review by the Joint Job Evaluation Committee** The Curriculum Multimedia Developer develops and deploys online interactive instructional multimedia for Open Learning courses and other on-campus groups.  This position supports and collaborates with other media and production specialists. The position manages the development and implementation of interactive multimedia in a variety of online formats. The Curriculum Multimedia Developer supports Instructional Designers, subject matter experts, and other faculty and staff with learning technologies and educational media. MAJOR DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Designs, develops, produces and coordinates implementation of responsive cross-platform interactive instructional multimedia and learning environments for Open Learning and campus, ensuring that they are fully adaptable to a wide variety of devices. Finds, repurposes and/or develops open educational multimedia resources under Creative Commons and related regimes; makes recommendations and participates in the development of storage and content sharing tools with the use of metadata systems and repositories. Oversees final implementation and quality control of multimedia, including testing and adjustments as necessary to ensure proper functioning of interactive multimedia including in live server environments. Supports and collaborates with graphics designer and video producer to achieve coordinated approaches to media development and implementation including providing assistance with basic video and graphic tasks when required. Based on a broad and in-depth knowledge of instructional media and technology, analyzes needs and makes recommendations to Instructional Designers, subject matter experts, faculty and staff on pedagogically sound interactive multimedia for online courses, programs and other educational offerings. Participates in course and program planning teams related to new development and maintenance of existing curriculum or other education focused projects, including handling of issues related to coordinating, scheduling and managing implementation of multiple projects under time-sensitive conditions. Utilizes project-tracking software and participates in constant quality improvement of  media team workflows related to the work with Instructional Design, Editing, Copyright and Production teams as well as campus clients . Operates in server environments for testing, production, and hosting of interactive educational multimedia, and communicates with technical server specialists concerning needs related to the smooth functioning and updating of host environments. Builds capacity in interactive multimedia by developing and delivering workshops and other hands-on training for campus and online faculty. Supports the Learning Technology and Innovation Team by identifying, analyzing, testing, evaluating, and reporting on existing and emerging learning media technologies and their appropriateness for use in online courses and programs, and in training others in the use of these technologies. Participates in relevant conferences by attending and presenting on practices and emerging developments in Open Learning and educational media. REPORTS TO Manager, Learning Technology and Innovation QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: Bachelor's degree in related field such as Digital Media/Arts; Learning Technologies; Instructional Development; Information Technology EXPERIENCE: Five years' related experience in an interactive multimedia role, including: Three years' experience in educational multi-media Two years working in a complex development and production setting requiring strong project management and coordination skills SKILLS KNOWLEDGE OR ABILITIES RELATED TO THE JOB Demonstrated proficiency in the following programing environments HTML5, CSS, JavaScript, PHP Demonstrated proficiency in user interface design and ability to create in multiple media formats (audio, video, and graphics) Demonstrated skills in e-learning, collaboration, and communication software such as WordPress, H5P, Articulate Storyline and Adobe Captivate Ability to create and edit sound, video and graphics media Ability to perform effectively as part of a project development team Ability to interpret curriculum requirements into appropriate educational interactive applications for LMS/external environments Communication and conflict management skills that are effective, courteous and tactful Ability to manage timelines using project management software for multiple concurrent and complex projects Ability to exercise considerable independent action and make sound decisions Advanced understanding of user interface design, media formats (audio, video, and graphics), and appropriate computer applications (e.g. current and emerging technologies) Understanding of how audio is recorded properly. Advanced knowledge of Adobe Creative Cloud suite Familiary with Camtasia video software Ability to operate in Windows server environment, web servers, , remote desk protocols and maintain best practices in workflow and file management Ability to work in Learning Management Systems (LMSs) e.g. Moodle Ability to use MS Office Suite WORKING CONDITIONS Sitting at a computer and desk for long periods of time General office conditions The salary for the above position is determined by the Collective Agreement with the Canadian Union of Public Employees, Local 4879, as it presently exists. Pay Band $34.07 - $37.86 ( CUPE Grade 09 (90% - 100%) ) Salary rate Please Note: This position may be subject to a 90% salary for the first 560 hours of employment. Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Open, Learning, Teaching and Innovation -> Innovations – OL Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job"
