    "https://tru.hua.hrsmart.com/hr/ats/Posting/view/34597": {
      "title": "Sessional - Faculty (PSYC 1110, 1210, & 3720) - (02050.11749)",
      "description": "Jump to main content Attention Safari users: This site requires cookies to function. Please click here to accept the cookie. Cookies will be used strictly for the functioning of the site. Toggle navigation Job Search View All Jobs Create Account Log in Help Help on this Page Job Details Sessional - Faculty (PSYC 1110, 1210, & 3720) - (02050.11749) Share this job as a link in your status update to LinkedIn. Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Faculty (Sessional) Posting In effect from 20/5/2026 Closing Application Date 3/6/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the closing application date and may continue until the position is filled. Instructional Type Academic/Career(max 24 credits) Anticipated Start Date 9/9/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) 28/4/2027 DUTIES The Department of Psychology is seeking sessional instructors to teach introductory psychology courses as well as upper-level courses in the area of social psychology/personality in 2026-2027, including PSYC 1110, PSYC 1210 and PSYC 3720 Special Topics (in the area of social psychology/personality, dependent on program requirements and instructor expertise). QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. in Psychology required, ABD may be considered. Post-secondary teaching experience. Pay Band $2,732.34 - $2,732.34 ( Sessional Faculty - Academic (per credit) ) Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 10 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Faculty of Arts -> Psychology Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualif